cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EnergetiScope in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "EnergetiScope: predicting Kubernetes workload energy consumption from workload specifications"
abstract: >-
  EnergetiScope predicts the energy consumption of a Kubernetes workload from its
  specification — image, resource requests, workload kind, and labels — before the workload
  runs. Ground-truth energy labels are collected from Kepler's eBPF power metrics via
  Prometheus. Workload specifications are encoded as a combination of optional SBERT text
  embeddings, numeric resource features, and one-hot categorical features, and a regressor is
  trained with workload-grouped cross-validation.
type: software
